        "id": 1308749
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-01T17:00:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is a single interrupt pin from the PDC for both ports, so they will always be the same.\n\nHowever, if we want to support more than 2 ports, that will require 2 separate PDC chips, each with their own interrupt.\n\nThis driver can validate that only 2 ports are present with a build assert  using `DT_NUM_INST_STATUS_OKAY(DT_DRV_COMPAT)`.\n\nSam - can you open a bug for supporting more than 2 ports with the RTS54xx driver?\n\nAs for modifying the devicetree binding, I think it\u0027s sufficient for now to validate that all ports use the interrupt.\n\nIt\u0027s probably possible to create some macrobatics to validate that all ports specify the same interrupt.  But a run-time check would be acceptable in the short term.\n\nSomething like\n```\nif (!irq_init_done) {\n    /* Existing code - configure GPIO and interrupt... */\n    shared_irq_gpio_port \u003d cfg-\u003eirq_gpios.port;\n    shared_irq_gpio_pin \u003d cfg-\u003eirq_gpios.pin;\n} else {\n    /* Validate this port matches IRQ settings */\n    if (cfg-\u003eirq_gpios.port !\u003d shared_irq_gpio_port)\n        return -EINVAL;\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "0a7b0ace_2e8b9cfd",
      "revId": "c3c165433da98230e4947f925a994156c003579b",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
